    <div class="ops-features-grid">

      <article class="ops-feature-block">
        <h3>Subscription Lifecycle Management for Fitness Studios</h3>
        <p>
          Running a gym means handling memberships that change state constantly — members
          upgrade plans, pause during holiday, miss a payment, or add a family member.
          Pagayo's subscription engine manages each state transition automatically:
          TRIALING starts a grace period, PAST_DUE triggers a dunning sequence, PAUSED
          suspends scan access without cancelling billing data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every member gets a unique pass code linked to their
          <code>subscriptionMember</code> record. The scan desk validates the pass in
          real time against the <code>subscriptionVisit</code> log — and blocks entry
          if the subscription is EXPIRED, CANCELED, or PAST_DUE.
        </p>
        <ul class="ops-bullet-list">
          <li>Automatic dunning — email reminders at 3, 7, and 14 days overdue</li>
          <li>Family memberships — multiple members per subscription holder</li>
          <li>Pause &amp; resume without losing payment history</li>
          <li>Upgrade and downgrade mid-cycle with pro-rata calculation</li>
          <li>Scan access log per member per day — full visit history</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="ops-feature-block">
        <h3>Integrated Gym POS and E-commerce Order Management</h3>
        <p>
          Most gym software treats the front desk and the webshop as separate systems.
          Pagayo uses one Order model for every sale channel: your receptionist selling a
          protein shake at the POS, a member buying a class pack online, or a coach
          accepting a walk-in payment via QR code — all land in the same order queue,
          with the same status flow.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <code>source</code> field (POS, WEB, CASH, WHATSAPP) and
          <code>originator</code> field (CUSTOMER, SELLER, SYSTEM) make every transaction
          auditable. Returns and refunds follow a four-stage process — requested, approved,
          received, refunded — with automatic credit note generation.
        </p>
        <ul class="ops-bullet-list">
          <li>Unified order queue — no separate POS and webshop reconciliation</li>
          <li>QR-code checkout for day passes and class packs</li>
          <li>Partial refunds and store credit</li>
          <li>VAT grouping per product category</li>
          <li>Daily end-of-day reconciliation report</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="ops-feature-block">
        <h3>Gym Stock, Coupons and Revenue Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          Beyond memberships and orders, gyms sell merchandise, supplements, and class packs.
          Pagayo tracks inventory per product variant, fires low-stock alerts when thresholds
          are crossed, and shows days-to-stockout estimates based on recent sales velocity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Coupon campaigns can be time-limited, member-segment specific, or tied to a
          referral source. Usage analytics per coupon code show redemption rate, average
          order uplift, and net revenue impact — so you can see which promotions actually
          drive revenue and which just erode margin.
        </p>
        <ul class="ops-bullet-list">
          <li>Inventory low-stock alerts with configurable thresholds</li>
          <li>Coupon codes — percentage or fixed, single-use or multi-use</li>
          <li>Revenue breakdown by membership vs. merchandise vs. classes</li>
          <li>Monthly recurring revenue (MRR) tracker</li>
          <li>Churn rate and net revenue retention per plan tier</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

